### 2.1 Do not confuse the release version with installed capabilities

Do not change the `installed.lock` contents solely to display v1.0.0. Record versions only after installing the corresponding verified source and passing migrations. The lock prevents reinstall; it is not proof of an audited codebase. A user-visible v0.7.x headline may coexist with v0.8/v0.9 modules in an incremental installation; the admin release manifest should report each independently.

## 3. Architecture and trust boundaries

### 3.1 Layered system diagram

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    U[Customer on phone or desktop] --> D[Merchant website / LMS / dApp]
    D --> S[JavaScript SDK / redirect integration]
    S <--> W[Dedicated HTTPS Coxy Wallet origin]
    W --> P[Public PHP API and OAuth gateway]
    P --> G[Tenant + permission + origin gates]
    G --> DB[(Private tenant / audit / payment database)]
    G --> SG[Signing request / payment intent policies]
    SG --> B[User-approved browser-side wallet / vault]
    B --> R[Allowlisted chain RPC gateway]
    R --> C[Cardano / Sepolia / network adapters]
    C --> N[(External testnet nodes and explorers)]
    N --> RE[Independent receipt and reconciliation verifier]
    RE --> DB
    OP[Administrator diagnostics and emergency stop] --> G
    OP --> R
```

This diagram illustrates the intended boundaries and integration flow, not a claim that every supported chain can already sign. The permission path runs *before* new payment or signing requests; the on-chain reconciliation path must be independent of browser callbacks.

### 3.2 The five security zones

1. **Merchant/dApp origin:** Treat arbitrary website JavaScript as untrusted. It can request permissions but must not access Coxy's decrypted keys.
2. **Dedicated wallet browser origin:** Secure customer authorization and, for applicable chains, user-side vault operations. Other applications must not share its origin; a different URL path is not isolation.
3. **Public PHP entrypoints:** Session/API routing, browser pages and a controlled same-origin RPC gateway. Public access must be minimized.
4. **Protected PHP/database layer:** Private configuration, tenant policy, payment state and audited server capabilities. Located outside all public document roots.
5. **External blockchain/network services:** Testnet RPC/indexer responses are untrusted until network ID, payload, units, recipient, amount and confirmation data are validated.

**Important custody clarification:** `coxy-wallet-private` is the private **server-code/config** directory. It is not where a website operator should collect customers' wallet recovery words. Merchant infrastructure credentials and operator-controlled service settings belong here; individual user signing material should remain protected by the wallet user's browser/device or an audited external wallet boundary.

### 3.3 Example dedicated-origin model

| Function | Example HTTPS origin | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Wallet | `https://wallet.example.org` | Secure account/consent interface |
| Merchant | `https://shop.example.org` | Customer checkout |
| LMS | `https://academy.example.org` | Course payments and Web3 identity |
| Test dApp | `https://demo.example.org` | Controlled integration tests |

All four are distinct browser origins. They can be administered by the same organization but should have independently managed document roots and deployment permissions. An origin is `scheme://hostname[:port]`; `/demo` is a path, not a new origin.

## 4. How the system works: the complete flows

### 4.1 User onboarding

The user opens the wallet over HTTPS, signs in and verifies their account. Depending on enabled features they may create or recover a wallet locally, choose an available testnet and view their public receive address. The backend should never ask the user to submit a recovery phrase for an administrator to store.

### 4.2 Registering a dApp

A platform admin creates a tenant (organization). A tenant owner or permitted administrator registers a dApp with its **exact HTTPS origin** and **exact callback URL**. The tenant controls the app's scopes and activation state. The server must prevent one origin from being claimed by two tenants and must prohibit new apps using the wallet origin itself. Website document-root independence must also be verified at the hosting level.

### 4.3 Consent, authorization and connection

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Dapp as Merchant / dApp
    participant Wallet as Coxy Wallet origin
    participant Auth as Tenant + OAuth API
    User->>Dapp: Click Connect Wallet
    Dapp->>Wallet: Authorization-code request + PKCE + state
    Wallet->>Auth: Validate origin, callback, tenant, scope, session
    Auth-->>Wallet: Allow only registered active app
    Wallet->>User: Display precise permissions
    User->>Wallet: Explicitly approve or reject
    Wallet-->>Dapp: One-time code at registered callback
    Dapp->>Auth: Redeem code with PKCE verifier
    Auth-->>Dapp: Restricted session / authorized account data
```

`address.read` permits only approved public-address access. `tx.request` is a **permission to request** a transaction, not permission to spend automatically. Every sensitive transaction must have a separate review and approval.

### 4.4 Merchant payment example

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Shop as Merchant server
    participant Wallet as Wallet application
    participant User as Customer
    participant RPC as Allowlisted chain provider
    participant Ledger as Merchant reconciliation
    Shop->>Ledger: Create unique order + signed payment intent
    Ledger-->>Shop: Prepared intent and expiry
    Shop->>Wallet: Customer-initiated checkout handoff
    Wallet->>User: Show chain, recipient, amount, fees
    User->>Wallet: Approve or cancel
    Wallet->>RPC: Broadcast only after valid signing approval
    RPC-->>Ledger: Transaction hash / receipt observations
    Ledger->>RPC: Verify status, amount, network and confirmations
    Ledger-->>Shop: Paid / pending / failed / uncertain state
```

**Never mark an order paid merely because a browser redirected back successfully.** Confirm the blockchain or provider settlement independently, and apply a per-chain finality/confirmation policy. If broadcast outcome is uncertain, reconcile first and **do not blindly resend**.

### 4.5 Suspending or revoking a tenant

Tenant policy must be checked at OAuth authorization, code exchange, token usage, signing creation, payment creation and merchant operation. Suspension blocks new sensitive actions and revokes usable authorizations. It does not reverse blockchain transactions already broadcast. History/reconciliation remains accessible to properly authorized operators for investigation.

## 5. Recommended folder structures

The actual uploaded packages use several internal paths. The directories below are the **deployed target layouts**, not a command to copy every preview ZIP over the same directory.

### 5.1 Layout A: dedicated wallet subdomain (preferred)

```text
hosting-account/
  domains/
    wallet.example.org/
      public_html/                     <-- HTTPS wallet document root
        .htaccess
        index.php
        wallet-loader.php
        api.php
        admin.php
        tenants.php
        authorize.php
        permissions.php
        sign.php
        pay.php
        evm.php                      (when installed from the working R3 base)
        adapters.php
        chain-read-api.php
        cardano-v080.php
        diagnostic-v070.php
        diagnostic-upgrade.php
        diagnostic-tenant-v090.php
        diagnostic-phase-b-v090.php
        assets/
          tenant-v090.mjs
          tenant-v090.css
          cardano-v080-panel.mjs
          ... other JS/CSS modules
        src/
          adapters.mjs
          midnight-lace.mjs
        sdk/
          coxy-connect.mjs
          coxy-connect.global.mjs
        demo/                         (staging only; never same-origin real dApp)
        install/                      (one-time fresh-install candidate only)
      coxy-wallet-private-isolated/    <-- sibling, NOT publicly served
        bootstrap.php
        settings.php
        installed.lock
        evm_testnet.php
        chain_readonly.php
        chain_readonly_extra.php
        dapp_permissions.php
        sign_api.php
