## 25. Release acceptance checklist

Mark these against **evidence**, not confidence or a screenshot of static diagnostic output.

### 25.1 Installation and recovery

- [ ] Dedicated wallet origin and its private sibling path independently verified.
- [ ] Fresh install on new empty database succeeds with complete migrations.
- [ ] Existing v0.9 installation upgrades without replacing live settings, accounts or historical records.
- [ ] PHP versions, extensions, MIME headers, TLS and outbound HTTPS validated on real host.
- [ ] Setup payload inaccessible/removed, `install/` locked, no SQL or private code downloadable.
- [ ] Signed package manifest and release hashes reviewed; backups and rollback exercised.

### 25.2 Authorization and tenant security

- [ ] Two independent tenants, origin claims, owners/admins/viewers tested.
- [ ] Cross-tenant object ID substitution fails in every relevant route.
- [ ] User consent, PKCE, state, exact callback and scope boundaries tested.
- [ ] Revocation and suspension immediately block new sensitive calls.
- [ ] Browser SDK never receives private merchant infrastructure secrets or customer signing material.

### 25.3 Wallet, money and chains

- [ ] Supported networks have exact identity/units and independently verified balance reads.
- [ ] Supported signers have actual user review, rejection and receipt tests.
- [ ] Merchant order identity is immutable and idempotent.
- [ ] Confirmation/reorg/failed/uncertain payments are reconciled, never decided by redirects.
- [ ] Mainnet emergency stop and per-chain feature flags pass negative tests.
- [ ] Real Android/iPhone device flows tested, including lost session and recovery.

### 25.4 Hosting distribution and external audit

- [ ] Canonical production source is fully integrated (no older EVM core regression).
- [ ] Softaculous metadata/install/archive/fileindex and upgrade callbacks reviewed.
- [ ] Licensed-host fresh install, upgrade, backup/restore and safe uninstall completed.
- [ ] Independent source/cryptography/API/security audit performed on exact release.
- [ ] Findings resolved and security contact, incident plan and update policy published.

If any P0 security item fails, the production/Mainnet release remains blocked.

